    "result_text": "There's a single test class and it passes, along with the full build. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required a new `telephoneDisplay` field: the stored E.164 `telephone` formatted for humans (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`), while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nI made three focused changes, reusing existing structure rather than duplicating logic:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerTelephones`** \u2014 added `toDisplay(String e164)`. This is the class that already owns all telephone-format knowledge (the recognised country calling codes and their national-number lengths), so it's the right home for the split-and-group formatting too. It reuses the existing `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` map to split the country code from the national digits, then groups the national part in threes. Made the class and method `public` so the mapper can reuse it (it stayed package-private before because only the function pipeline used it).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay(owner)` helper and a `@Mapping` expression, alongside the other derived-field mappings (`displayName`, `initials`, etc.), delegating to `OwnerTelephones.toDisplay`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` passes and the full build is green.",
